# Copilot Instructions

## General Guidelines
- Ensure visual consistency across the website.
- Apply the same CSS styling and theme variables from `index.html` to `survey2.html`, maintaining the dark theme, spacing system, colors, and animations.
- Use the visual style from `index_en.html` for the landing container to ensure consistent branding.
- Initialize Firebase directly via `firebase-config.js` instead of using `.env.local` or Vite/VITE_* variables to simplify project setup and reduce complexity. Use a single Firebase project for streamlined management.
- Focus exclusively on HTML, CSS, and JavaScript changes; avoid any C language code.
- Implement in-app Firestore messaging flow instead of using Mailgun for email delivery, streamlining communication within the application.
- Ensure the envelope unread badge implementation is secure and visible only to logged-in users, preventing exposure to signed-out users.

## Insights Archive Guidelines
- Prioritize topic tags in the following order: ESG, Energy, and Real Estate.

## CSS/JS Synchronization
- Ensure seamless CSS/JS synchronization for the search bar, cookie consent banner, and chatbot popup, styled consistently with `index_en.html`.
- Prioritize smooth transitions, consistent branding, and accessible behavior across all interactive elements.
- Ensure the chatbot popup header covers the entire popup with a blue gradient, and style footer links precisely for a polished appearance.